  "narrative": {
    "intro": "California Institute of Technology obligated $1.7B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. California Institute of Technology recorded 337 awards, with an average award size of $5M. California Institute of Technology obligations are down 26.6% year over year. California Institute of Technology yearly obligations trended from $2.3B in FY21 to $2.6B in FY22, $2.7B in FY23, $2.2B in FY24, $2.3B in FY25, and $1.7B in FY26. California Institute of Technology is concentrated in research and development markets, with Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $1.7B. FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date, so the FY26 figure represents a partial year of obligations. This profile highlights award count, average award size, and market concentration in R&D categories that matter to contractors and agency buyers tracking Caltech activity.",
